<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    SSR (purple) and UR (red): the top two tiers. See MoreStorylikeTraits.xml for the whole scale.

    Most of these carry a long <disallowedInspirations> list, which is the author's way of saying
    "this person is only ever inspired about one thing". Read the list by what is MISSING from it:
    the entries are what the pawn can never be inspired to do, so the one or two vanilla
    inspirations absent from the list are the only ones left. Each description below says which
    one that is, checked against the list rather than against the original English text - the 1.3
    English got several of them backwards.
  -->

  <!-- ============================ SSR - purple ============================ -->

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR01ThePersonInDream</defName><!-- 梦境中人 -->
    <commonality>0.05</commonality>
    <commonalityFemale>0.12</commonalityFemale>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>the person in dreams</label>
        <description>Form is emptiness, and what {PAWN_nameDef} actually looks like turns out not to matter. It would be too much to say that everyone has met {PAWN_objective} in a dream. It is simply the case that everyone, on meeting {PAWN_objective}, is glad to.</description>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR02RuthlessWorkMachine</defName><!-- 无情的工作机器 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>ruthless work machine</label>
        <description>In every colony {PAWN_nameDef} has ever been part of, {PAWN_pronoun} was the one who worked hardest. When things go well {PAWN_pronoun} works. When things go badly {PAWN_pronoun} breaks down, and then {PAWN_pronoun} works, because the situation will not improve on its own. Nothing inspires {PAWN_objective} but work, and {PAWN_pronoun} comes out of a breakdown straight into it.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <WorkSpeedGlobal>0.6</WorkSpeedGlobal>
          <MentalBreakThreshold>0.15</MentalBreakThreshold>
        </statOffsets>
        <disallowedInspirations>
          <li>Frenzy_Go</li>
          <li>Inspired_Creativity</li>
          <li>Frenzy_Shoot</li>
          <li>Inspired_Trade</li>
          <li>Inspired_Recruitment</li>
          <li>Inspired_Taming</li>
          <li>Inspired_Surgery</li>
        </disallowedInspirations>
        <disallowedMentalStates>
          <li>CorpseObsession</li>
          <li>TargetedInsultingSpree</li>
          <li>SocialFighting</li>
          <li>FireStartingSpree</li>
        </disallowedMentalStates>
        <mentalBreakInspirationGainSet>
          <li>Frenzy_Work</li>
        </mentalBreakInspirationGainSet>
        <mentalBreakInspirationGainChance>1</mentalBreakInspirationGainChance>
        <socialFightChanceFactor>0</socialFightChanceFactor>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>HYPSR03JustMoreWonders</li>
      <li>HYPN01FinelyCrafted</li>
      <li>HYPSR13SoManyIdea</li>
      <li>HYPSSR05TheUltimateBricklayer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR06BloodthirstyViking</li>
      <li>HYPSSR07FieldSniper</li>
      <li>HYPSSR10YuZuSoftFan</li>
      <li>HYPSSR12DolphinVoiceTalent</li>
      <li>HYPSSR14ArtZoneDivision</li>
      <li>HYPSSR15MasterOfNegotiations</li>
      <li>HYPUR03TheDealWithLucifer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR13FirearmsExpert</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>PlantWork</li>
      <li>Crafting</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR03PetrochemicalSkin</defName><!-- 石化皮肤 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>petrified skin</label>
        <description>{PAWN_nameDef}'s skin has hardened, in patches and then in sheets, into something closer to slate than to flesh. People do not like to look at it and are worse at hiding that than they think. Blades turn on it, and so does fire.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <PawnBeauty>-1</PawnBeauty>
          <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.5</ArmorRating_Sharp>
          <ArmorRating_Heat>0.5</ArmorRating_Heat>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>HYPUR01CrystallizedSkin</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR04StupidAsStupidDoes</defName><!-- 傻人傻福 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>fools have all the luck</label>
        <description>Ask {PAWN_nameDef} to think about anything and the day is lost. Ask {PAWN_objective} to do it instead and it comes out right, every time, for no reason anyone can name: the vein is richer, the harvest is fuller, the patient wakes up. {PAWN_pronoun} has never once wondered why.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <ImmunityGainSpeed>0.2</ImmunityGainSpeed>
          <MiningYield>0.25</MiningYield>
          <PlantHarvestYield>0.25</PlantHarvestYield>
          <AnimalGatherYield>0.25</AnimalGatherYield>
          <ConstructSuccessChance>0.25</ConstructSuccessChance>
          <MedicalSurgerySuccessChance>0.25</MedicalSurgerySuccessChance>
          <TameAnimalChance>0.25</TameAnimalChance>
          <TrainAnimalChance>0.25</TrainAnimalChance>
          <ResearchSpeed>-0.95</ResearchSpeed>
        </statOffsets>
        <skillGains>
          <Intellectual>-20</Intellectual>
        </skillGains>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>HYPR15OfCourseUseful</li>
      <li>HYPSR12ObviouslyAndClearly</li>
      <li>HYPUR04SuperArtificialIntelligence</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>Crafting</li>
      <li>Caring</li>
      <li>Artistic</li>
      <li>Animals</li>
      <li>PlantWork</li>
      <li>Mining</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR05TheUltimateBricklayer</defName><!-- 究极搬砖工 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>ultimate brick-hauler</label>
        <description>On the site they called {PAWN_objective} the ultimate brick-hauler, and meant it literally: {PAWN_nameDef} carries several times what anyone else can and walks faster doing it. A researcher once asked, politely, for a blood sample. The results were returned marked inconclusive and the researcher stopped answering letters. Nothing inspires {PAWN_objective} but the road.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <MoveSpeed>0.8</MoveSpeed>
          <CarryingCapacity>125</CarryingCapacity>
        </statOffsets>
        <disallowedInspirations>
          <li>Inspired_Creativity</li>
          <li>Frenzy_Work</li>
          <li>Frenzy_Shoot</li>
          <li>Inspired_Trade</li>
          <li>Inspired_Recruitment</li>
          <li>Inspired_Taming</li>
          <li>Inspired_Surgery</li>
        </disallowedInspirations>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>HYPSR03JustMoreWonders</li>
      <li>HYPN01FinelyCrafted</li>
      <li>HYPSR13SoManyIdea</li>
      <li>HYPSSR07FieldSniper</li>
      <li>HYPSSR10YuZuSoftFan</li>
      <li>HYPSSR12DolphinVoiceTalent</li>
      <li>HYPSSR14ArtZoneDivision</li>
      <li>HYPSSR15MasterOfNegotiations</li>
      <li>HYPUR03TheDealWithLucifer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR02RuthlessWorkMachine</li>
      <li>HYPSSR13FirearmsExpert</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>Crafting</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR06BloodthirstyViking</defName><!-- 嗜血维京 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Melee</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>bloodthirsty viking</label>
        <description>The bloodlust runs in {PAWN_nameDef}'s family the way a nose does, and {PAWN_pronoun} is no exception to it. {PAWN_possessive} way of attacking is famous among people who have survived it: {PAWN_pronoun} does not defend, {PAWN_pronoun} arrives. Hand {PAWN_objective} a rifle and {PAWN_pronoun} will sulk. Nothing inspires {PAWN_objective} but the charge, and {PAWN_pronoun} eats like it.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <MoveSpeed>0.5</MoveSpeed>
          <WorkSpeedGlobal>-0.1</WorkSpeedGlobal>
          <MeleeHitChance>18</MeleeHitChance>
          <MeleeDodgeChance>18</MeleeDodgeChance>
          <IncomingDamageFactor>0.2</IncomingDamageFactor>
          <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.3</ArmorRating_Sharp>
          <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.3</ArmorRating_Blunt>
          <HungerRateMultiplier>0.3</HungerRateMultiplier>
        </statOffsets>
        <statFactors>
          <MeleeDPS>1.5</MeleeDPS>
        </statFactors>
        <skillGains>
          <Melee>5</Melee>
        </skillGains>
        <disallowedInspirations>
          <li>Inspired_Creativity</li>
          <li>Frenzy_Work</li>
          <li>Frenzy_Shoot</li>
          <li>Inspired_Trade</li>
          <li>Inspired_Recruitment</li>
          <li>Inspired_Taming</li>
          <li>Inspired_Surgery</li>
        </disallowedInspirations>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>HYPSR03JustMoreWonders</li>
      <li>HYPN01FinelyCrafted</li>
      <li>HYPSR13SoManyIdea</li>
      <li>HYPR04MasterSection</li>
      <li>HYPSR01NeverCheat</li>
      <li>HYPSSR07FieldSniper</li>
      <li>HYPSSR10YuZuSoftFan</li>
      <li>HYPSSR12DolphinVoiceTalent</li>
      <li>HYPSSR14ArtZoneDivision</li>
      <li>HYPSSR15MasterOfNegotiations</li>
      <li>HYPUR03TheDealWithLucifer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR13FirearmsExpert</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>Violent</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR07FieldSniper</defName><!-- 战地狙击手 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Shooting</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>field sniper</label>
        <description>The reason {PAWN_nameDef} is still alive is not the rifle, it is the suit: a bundle of scrim and local weeds that has taken more rounds than {PAWN_pronoun} has. Fire at where {PAWN_pronoun} appears to be and you hit the ghillie, while {PAWN_pronoun} lies somewhere behind it holding {PAWN_possessive} breath and waiting for you to reload.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <WorkSpeedGlobal>-0.1</WorkSpeedGlobal>
          <ShootingAccuracyPawn>12</ShootingAccuracyPawn>
          <AimingDelayFactor>-0.3</AimingDelayFactor>
          <HuntingStealth>0.6</HuntingStealth>
          <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.6</ArmorRating_Sharp>
          <ArmorRating_Heat>0.6</ArmorRating_Heat>
        </statOffsets>
        <skillGains>
          <Shooting>5</Shooting>
        </skillGains>
        <disallowedInspirations>
          <li>Frenzy_Go</li>
          <li>Inspired_Trade</li>
          <li>Inspired_Recruitment</li>
          <li>Inspired_Taming</li>
          <li>Inspired_Surgery</li>
        </disallowedInspirations>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <!--
        The 1.3 file listed HYPUR03TheDealWithLucifer twice here. Duplicates are harmless -
        RimWorld only ever asks whether a def is in the list - but there is no reason to keep one.
      -->
      <li>Brawler</li>
      <li>HYPSR03JustMoreWonders</li>
      <li>HYPSSR14ArtZoneDivision</li>
      <li>HYPSSR05TheUltimateBricklayer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR10YuZuSoftFan</li>
      <li>HYPSSR06BloodthirstyViking</li>
      <li>HYPSSR02RuthlessWorkMachine</li>
      <li>HYPUR03TheDealWithLucifer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR12DolphinVoiceTalent</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>Violent</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR08InfrastructureSpree</defName><!-- 基建狂魔 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Construction</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>infrastructure maniac</label>
        <description>Something happened to {PAWN_nameDef} as a child and nobody has ever got the story out of {PAWN_objective}. What is certain is the result. "Infrastructure is everything," {PAWN_pronoun} says, without being asked. "I dream about it a lot."</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <SmoothingSpeed>0.75</SmoothingSpeed>
          <ConstructionSpeed>0.75</ConstructionSpeed>
          <ConstructSuccessChance>0.50</ConstructSuccessChance>
        </statOffsets>
        <skillGains>
          <Construction>5</Construction>
        </skillGains>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>ManualSkilled</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR09Excavator</defName><!-- 地质学家 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Mining</li>
      <li>Intellectual</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>geologist</label>
        <description>A medieval treatise on rimworld geology fell into {PAWN_nameDef}'s hands, and {PAWN_pronoun} has read it so many times that stone no longer looks solid to {PAWN_objective}. However stubborn the face, {PAWN_pronoun} sees a few pieces that came apart a long time ago and have simply not been told.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <MiningSpeed>0.75</MiningSpeed>
          <MiningYield>0.5</MiningYield>
        </statOffsets>
        <skillGains>
          <Mining>4</Mining>
          <Intellectual>2</Intellectual>
        </skillGains>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>Crafting</li>
      <li>Intellectual</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR10YuZuSoftFan</defName><!-- 柚子厨 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Cooking</li>
      <li>Artistic</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>visual novel devotee</label>
        <description>{PAWN_nameDef} has opinions about one small studio's back catalogue and will share them at length, mostly in threads nobody asked for. Somewhere in all that devotion {PAWN_pronoun} also learned to cook and to draw, properly, at a level that embarrasses people who trained for it. Only work and a good idea will ever inspire {PAWN_objective}, and {PAWN_pronoun} does not mind the heat of a kitchen at all.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <CookSpeed>1.50</CookSpeed>
          <FoodPoisonChance>-0.25</FoodPoisonChance>
          <ComfyTemperatureMax>10</ComfyTemperatureMax>
        </statOffsets>
        <skillGains>
          <Cooking>4</Cooking>
          <Artistic>4</Artistic>
        </skillGains>
        <disallowedInspirations>
          <li>Frenzy_Go</li>
          <li>Frenzy_Shoot</li>
          <li>Inspired_Trade</li>
          <li>Inspired_Recruitment</li>
          <li>Inspired_Taming</li>
          <li>Inspired_Surgery</li>
        </disallowedInspirations>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>HYPSSR02RuthlessWorkMachine</li>
      <li>HYPSSR05TheUltimateBricklayer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR06BloodthirstyViking</li>
      <li>HYPSSR07FieldSniper</li>
      <li>HYPSSR12DolphinVoiceTalent</li>
      <li>HYPSSR14ArtZoneDivision</li>
      <li>HYPSSR15MasterOfNegotiations</li>
      <li>HYPUR03TheDealWithLucifer</li>
      <li>HYPSSR13FirearmsExpert</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>Cooking</li>
      <li>Artistic</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR11TheSecretSeedsOfEAAS</defName><!-- 农科院的秘密种子 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Plants</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>academy seeds</label>
        <description>Somebody at the Empire's local academy of agricultural sciences owes {PAWN_nameDef} a favour, or is owed one, and the arrangement is not written down anywhere. What arrives is seed stock that should not be in civilian hands: it comes up where nothing comes up, and it comes up heavy.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <PlantWorkSpeed>0.75</PlantWorkSpeed>
          <PlantHarvestYield>0.5</PlantHarvestYield>
        </statOffsets>
        <skillGains>
          <Plants>5</Plants>
        </skillGains>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <requiredWorkTags>
      <li>PlantWork</li>
    </requiredWorkTags>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>HYPSSR12DolphinVoiceTalent</defName><!-- 海豚音天赋 -->
    <commonality>0.1</commonality>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Animals</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>dolphin voice</label>
        <description>{PAWN_nameDef}'s ears and throat are not built like other people's. {PAWN_pronoun} hears an octave above the rest of the colony and can answer in it, which makes talking to an animal less a matter of training than of conversation. Nothing inspires {PAWN_objective} but a creature that has not been tamed yet.</description>
        <statOffsets>
          <TrainAnimalChance>0.75</TrainAnimalChance>
          <TameAnimalChance>0.5</TameAnimalChance>
          <AnimalGatherYield>0.25</AnimalGatherYield>
